WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.900
A Notice from the Yamayuri Council
When watching
"Maria Watches Over Us ~Printemps~,"
please have the room brightly lit and
sit well away from the television set.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:17.440
Maria Watches Over Us
Printemps

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:26.520
In the morning mist,
Asamoya no naka

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:33.460
the white path goes on.
tsuzuku shiroi michi

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:40.930
The birds sing.
Tori no saezuri

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:48.600
We exchange greetings.
Aisatsu kawashinagara

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:56.080
At times, the clouds hang low,
Toki ni kumo ga tarekomete

00:00:56.650 --> 00:01:03.560
and the sun may grow dim.
hizashi kagerou tomo

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:11.630
But I will walk with my chin up,
Sesuji nobashite aruku

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:19.140
for I know,
watashi wa shitteru kara

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:26.180
that above those heavy clouds...
omoi kumo no ue wa

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:34.110
...is the blue sky.
aoi sora

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:16.930
Yumi-san...

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:20.130
Is there anything for me to do?

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:22.300
"Anything"?

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.330
There are too many things to do,

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:26.210
School Festival

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:28.200
School Festival
so I don't even know where to begin...

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:32.170
I guess getting ready for the
school festival is hard work.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.940
Sachiko-sama is absent...

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:37.980
...and Rei-sama and Yoshino-san seem
busy with the Kendo Team.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:41.720
Why not ask the school festival
executive committee for help?

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:47.950
In that case, I would rather have either
you or Yoshino-san find a little sister.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:57.600
Shimako-san has become
much more like a Lady Rose.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:01.640
Once Rei-sama's kendo obligations taper off,

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.410
and Sachiko-sama returns to school,

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.170
I think we will be able to manage.

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:11.450
But I wonder what in the world
is going on with Sachiko-sama.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:13.680
I know...

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:19.750
It seems something has
happened to Rosa Chinensis.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.020
Something? Like what?
Something? Like what?

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:24.430
I don't know...

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.860
I did try asking, but...

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.530
Toko refuses to say, so...

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.000
Toko-chan, huh?

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:36.910
I'm sorry I couldn't be of help, Yumi-sama.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.910
No, it's okay. Thank you.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:42.180
At any rate,

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.350
our current issue is that
we're shorthanded, right?

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:47.650
Still, regardless of all that,

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.150
I'm glad that you're back to your old self.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.570
What might this be about?

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:08.900
First, could I ask you to relax
your combative attitude?

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.810
Didn't you summon me out here
to press me for answers...

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:15.610
...or to air your grievances?

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:19.520
I want to ask you to help out
with the Yamayuri Council.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:22.720
P-Pardon?

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:27.260
Rosa Foetida has a lot of new
members on the Kendo Team...

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:29.060
...and since all of them are novices,

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.930
it seems their training is keeping her busy.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:35.060
That will likely keep up
for the rest of this term, so...

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:38.610
I'm part of the Drama Club, too...

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:42.270
So, you can just help when
you have no club obligations.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.410
What are you doing?

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:51.090
Escorting you to the Rose Mansion.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:58.250
I will help out. But only while
Rosa Chinensis is absent.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:00.190
Really? Thank you.

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:07.040
Using touch to communicate
like I learned from Sei-sama...

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.430
Maybe it's effective.

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:16.710
And maybe we were also
able to debunk the rumor...

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.310
...that Toko-chan and I are
fighting over my Onee-sama.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:24.440
A week has gone by since then,

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.080
but Sachiko-sama still hasn't returned to school.

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:30.220
Toko-chan.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:33.450
Sorry, but could you make copies of these?

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:37.290
I guess you're actually rather cold, Yumi-sama.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:38.690
What?

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.170
Sachiko-sama has been absent all this time,

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:42.800
but you're not going to do anything?

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:46.730
That's why I'm working hard here, though.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:49.340
That isn't what I'm talking about.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.230
Rosa Foetida.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:52.810
What is it?

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:55.140
Please switch seats with me!

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:59.480
Being next to Yumi-sama isn't
good for my mental health!

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:00.820
No.

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:02.510
Why not?!

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:07.690
The reason is because you're
a helper that Yumi-chan brought in.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:11.830
Sorry, but we weren't involved whatsoever.

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:27.510
Please don't follow me!

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.510
Wait for me, Toko-chan.

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:31.980
I don't understand you at all, Yumi-sama!

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:35.790
Just a week ago, you were
almost infuriatingly downcast,

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:37.820
but now you're suddenly recovered!

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:41.530
You don't like it when I'm cheerful?

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:45.800
I'm an eyesore to you! So why go to
the trouble of keeping me around?!

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:50.300
I thought someone else who loves
Sachiko-sama should be the one...

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.570
...to work hard in her absence.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:59.240
That's why I went back
to the Rose Mansion, too.

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:04.420
Because we both love her?

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:06.880
What are you saying at this late date?

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:10.220
After you ran away without hearing
what Sachiko Onee-sama had to say!

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:16.490
But I mean, I really don't know
what's going on with my Onee-sama.

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:28.810
My, is that you, Yumi-san?

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:31.270
Good day.

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:33.370
Good day, Yumiko-san.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:35.880
Are you on your way home from somewhere?

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:37.450
No, quite the opposite.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:40.210
I found out where an old friend of mine is,

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.480
so I'm thinking of going to see her.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:47.330
So I just went to tell Kei-san
that I'd be away for a while.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.320
Your friend?

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:55.400
Long ago, we quarreled over a trifling matter.

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:58.630
But now I'm going to reconcile with her.

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:00.570
This parasol...

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.570
It's an old parasol, isn't it?

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.300
But I couldn't bring myself to throw it away.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:09.510
It's the parasol I had when I last saw her.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:14.020
That day, I was unable to say that I was sorry.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.520
So I plan to go and say it now.

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:19.990
But...

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:22.420
I wonder what she will say...

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:26.170
Well, I think I'll be on my way now.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:36.230
Is it far?

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:39.280
Yes, but I'll be fine.

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:41.540
My destination is a hospital.

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:45.250
Even if something should happen,
they can take care of me there.

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:50.150
So, Yumiko-san's friend is hospitalized...

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:00.430
A hospital, huh?

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:01.160
What?

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:04.410
My grandfather runs a small hospital
at the base of a mountain...

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.500
...in a prefecture near Tokyo.

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:08.810
You can only get there by car,

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:11.370
but there's a lot of greenery and the air's fresh.

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:13.440
Could it be?

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:16.270
Is that where Sachiko-sama
is being hospitalized?

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:21.290
You are so simple-minded, Yumi-sama.

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:25.880
Didn't you know that Sachiko-sama
isn't absent due to illness?

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.050
Then...

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:29.830
This conversation ends here.

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:34.430
Even if I do nothing,
someone will surely act soon anyway.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:36.830
What do you mean, Toko-chan?

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:41.530
I shall give you one word of advice,
Yumi-sama.

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:42.640
What?

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:48.780
You should do your best not to get in
a car driven by Suguru Nii-sama.

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:51.510
By Kashiwagi-san? What's that about?

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:55.210
If you aren't used to it,
you'll get motion sickness.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:58.120
Especially on unpaved roads.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:52.050
High school division, Year 2,
Pine Class, Fukuzawa Yumi-san,

00:10:52.180 --> 00:10:54.310
please come to the faculty office immediately.

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:56.780
I repeat.

00:10:56.780 --> 00:10:59.720
High school division, Year 2,
Pine Class, Fukuzawa Yumi-san,

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:01.710
please come to the faculty office immediately.

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:18.170
Yumi-san, why?

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:19.370
Why what?

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:21.400
The arrival at the school gate.

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:23.070
Whose arrival?

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:30.710
The prince's arrival.

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:33.120
In a bright-red pumpkin sports car.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:35.850
Kashiwagi-san is here?

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:44.530
Yumi-san...

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:48.490
They've all come here out of concern for me...

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:52.400
Good day, Yumi-chan.

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:57.140
Rosa Chinensis!

00:11:58.110 --> 00:11:59.100
Long time no see.

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:02.370
W-What in the world are you doing here?

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:04.080
I came for you.

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:05.610
Come with me.

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:10.110
What? Then it was Rosa
Chinensis who had me summoned?

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:12.360
Tell me, Yumi-chan,

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:15.860
would you be willing to help Sachiko for me?

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:20.630
I would.

00:12:21.270 --> 00:12:22.200
Then, come with me.

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:26.300
Yumi-san.

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:28.600
Here.

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:31.280
Thank you.

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:33.680
Hang in there.

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:35.910
You can tell me all about it later.

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:37.810
Right.

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:53.730
This isn't the usual supremely
confident, utterly serene Yoko-sama.

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:55.830
What could have happened?

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:59.040
Um, Yoko-sama, I'm sorry...

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:03.880
You asked me to take care of
Sachiko-sama, and yet...

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:08.410
I'm sure it was Sachiko's fault.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:10.110
But...

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:13.190
Even if you had lost patience with Sachiko,

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:14.980
I'd think it couldn't have been helped.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:18.420
But right now, I want you to come with me.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:20.960
And I want you to help Sachiko.

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:24.930
Even though I've graduated,

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:27.960
I'll probably be her big sister
for the rest of my life.

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:30.460
Go ahead and say a prayer.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:32.930
What about you, Yoko-sama?

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:36.740
I'll refrain for today. I said my
prayers somewhere else already.

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:43.210
Yumi-chan.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:44.480
Yes?

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:47.280
Do you love Sachiko?

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:50.050
Yes.

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:53.690
I see. I'm glad.

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:56.060
Come, let's go.

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:57.990
Our driver is waiting, too.

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:04.270
I've been waiting for you, Cinderella.

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:15.910
Are you all right?

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:21.160
The other day, when I took
Sacchan to the hospital,

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:23.390
she told me she'd never ride with me again.

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:24.860
The hospital?

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:29.130
Yes, Sacchan's grandmother was hospitalized.

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:33.520
Sayako Oba-sama's mother, you see...

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:37.560
My Onee-sama's grandmother...

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:41.080
It seems Sacchan's been going
to see her pretty frequently...

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:43.130
...this last month.

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:45.840
Once when the Ogasawara car was unavailable,

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:49.640
I took Sacchan to the hospital in my car, but...

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:54.150
...on that occasion, Toko insisted on
coming along and wouldn't listen...

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:58.480
...since it's the hospital her grandfather runs.

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:02.590
Come to think of it,
you called that day, didn't you?

00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:04.100
Oh!

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:04.760
Whoops...

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:09.730
Excuse me, Mr. Driver,

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:13.030
keep your eyes forward
and concentrate on driving.

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:28.250
3-Chome Intersection

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:31.990
Then, Sachiko-sama is at the hospital?

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:37.720
Our destination isn't the hospital.

00:15:38.070 --> 00:15:38.830
What?

00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:40.990
Today was the funeral.

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:46.400
Because her grandmother had
wanted a private family funeral,

00:15:46.970 --> 00:15:50.640
Kashiwagi-san and I both just went
to see Sachiko this morning...

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:52.270
...to offer our condolences.

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:53.810
It was her will.

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:58.510
She probably didn't want
the funeral to be a big deal.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:11.300
Where are we?

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:12.970
Her grandmother's residence.

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:18.330
Oh, Yumi-chan. I am so sorry about this.

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:20.260
Thank you for coming.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.880
Not at all. May I offer my...

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:23.930
No, no, it's all right.

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:26.040
Just come in.

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:29.150
Oba-sama, I shall go look at the garden.

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:31.280
Then, I think I'll keep you company.

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:41.650
Would you please go see Sachiko?

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:49.330
Please pardon my intrusion.

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:56.530
Up until my mother passed away,
I was weeping all the time.

00:16:57.010 --> 00:17:00.140
It seems I've since run out of tears.

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:03.780
I'm fine now. Back to my old self.

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:13.220
Since my mother's passing,
I've been able to let it go,

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:16.460
but like a strained thread that has snapped,

00:17:16.460 --> 00:17:18.290
Sachiko's grown despondent.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:21.040
I was crying all the time,

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:23.830
so she was straining herself to be strong for me.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:28.140
Not knowing what to do,
I asked Yoko-san to come, but...

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:32.510
She said there was nothing she could do.

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:36.080
Beyond those doors.

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:49.920
Please go to her.

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:53.630
I will.

00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:26.490
Onee-sama...

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:33.330
Am I dreaming?

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:05.370
Is this a dream?

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:07.240
No.

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:11.940
No, Onee-sama, I'm here.

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:13.850
It's you, isn't it, Yumi?

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:16.580
I'm sorry, Onee-sama.

00:19:16.650 --> 00:19:18.990
I was being so selfish and
making things difficult for you...

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:21.450
...when you were having such a tough time.

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:26.780
You did nothing wrong, Yumi. It was my fault.

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:36.700
Onee-sama...

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:39.230
So you'll still call me that?

00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:41.030
Of course.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:43.410
Will you forgive me?

00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:45.080
Forgive?

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:47.270
I wish you had just told me.

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:49.820
I couldn't tell you,

00:19:49.820 --> 00:19:52.920
because when I thought of my
grandmother when I was with you,

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.650
I felt as though I would cry.

00:19:56.560 --> 00:20:00.520
I thought you would understand,
even if I said nothing.

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:03.060
But I was taking you for granted.

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:06.630
You're also capable of
being hurt and disillusioned.

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:10.600
What kind of a Onee-sama am I,
that I didn't even realize that.

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:15.470
Since I've been crying so much,

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:18.870
my grandmother must have brought you to me.

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:22.150
Before she passed away,

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:24.780
she was able to see someone she
had really wanted to see, you know.

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:28.620
They had quarreled and
parted ways a long time ago,

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:32.680
so it seems she thought she'd
never get to see her again.

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:39.820
Is this...

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:41.700
Is this a dream?

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:48.870
No, I am here.

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:50.810
So it is you.

00:20:51.210 --> 00:20:52.470
I am sorry.

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:58.480
I was so very selfish and
made things difficult for you.

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:04.220
No, you did nothing wrong. It was my fault.

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:08.750
It seems she was suddenly
reminded of my grandmother.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:11.930
My grandmother's wish must have reached her.

00:21:12.970 --> 00:21:16.530
A short while later,
my grandmother passed away,

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:19.400
but she looked very happy.

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:28.610
How do I look right now?

00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:30.610
Onee-sama...

00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:33.540
I love you.

00:23:00.670 --> 00:23:04.610
With a Parasol

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:16.250
Onee-sama,

00:23:16.960 --> 00:23:18.980
I, too...

00:23:20.730 --> 00:23:22.020
...love you, very much.
